WARDEN_USAGE=$(cat <<'USAGE'
\033[33mUsage:\033[0m
  d1-backup [label]              Exports the LOCAL D1 database to backups/d1-ledger-<timestamp>-<label>.sql
  d1-backup --remote [label]     Exports the LIVE Cloudflare D1 database to backups/d1-ledger-remote-<timestamp>-<label>.sql
                                 (read only: nothing on Cloudflare is changed)

  Warden 0.16 rejects a bare --remote, so put -- before it:
    warden d1-backup -- --remote before-change

  --remote needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID in .env.
  The label is just a name (not a path): backups/x.sql becomes the label x.
  Each file gets a .sha256 beside it. Restore one locally with: warden d1-restore <file>

\033[33mOptions:\033[0m
  -h, --help        Display this help menu
USAGE
)
